<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Appendix</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Related Work</h3>

<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Test-time Scaling.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recent works explore <span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">test-time scaling</span>—the idea that increasing computation during inference can be more effective than scaling model size <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">Snell et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wu et al., 2024</a>)</cite>. A common strategy is <span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">sequential scaling</span>, adopted in models like OpenAI o1 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">OpenAI, 2024</a>)</cite> and DeepSeek R1 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Guo et al., 2025</a>)</cite>. Other approaches <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Muennighoff et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yan et al., 2025</a>)</cite> use supervised fine-tuning to match a fixed compute budget. In parallel, <span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">parallel scaling</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib48" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zeng et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Pan et al., 2025a</a>)</cite> improves throughput by distributing inference across replicas or devices, offering latency gains but introducing challenges in memory overhead.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Speculative decoding</h4>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Speculative decoding<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">(</span><a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., 2024a</a>; <a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Leviathan et al., 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kim et al., 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al., 2023</a><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">)</span></cite></span> is an emerging technique for accelerating LLM inference, which is traditionally limited by slow, sequential autoregressive sampling and memory bandwidth constraints. There are three main strategies for sampling draft tokens: <span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">token-level sampling<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">(</span><a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Leviathan et al., 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kim et al., 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al., 2023</a><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">)</span></cite></span>, where the large model directly verifies the token outputs of the draft model; <span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">feature-level sampling</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cai et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., 2024a</a>; <a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., 2024b</a>)</cite>, which verifies generation paths using intermediate representations; and <span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">step-level sampling</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">Pan et al., 2025b</a>; <a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, which operates at a coarser granularity by validating multiple tokens or computation steps together to improve throughput.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Asynchronous Tool Calling.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The synchronization issue in batch inference with tool calls <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhu et al., 2025</a>)</cite> is a known obstacle to efficient reasoning. However, it remains underexplored in the context of speculative decoding—particularly when large model inference is treated as a form of tool call. In asynchronous scheduling, controlling the frequency of large model intervention is challenging due to synchronization overhead. Recent approaches <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ginart et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gonzalez-Pumariega et al., 2025</a>)</cite> employ event-driven finite-state machine architectures to manage asynchronous tool calls more flexibly and efficiently.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Conformal Prediction.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To avoid synchronization and to accurately predict the request budget in the scaling process, we introduce conformal prediction <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Derhacobian et al., </a>; <a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Angelopoulos et al., 2020</a>; <a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Huang et al., 2023</a>)</cite> to provide a theoretical guarantee for the budget of times our target model intervenes. The prediction set is then used to ensure that the large model’s interventions remain consistent with the desired coverage and reliability, aligning with the validation process. However, these methods all require the model to perform a complete softmax operation (which requires synchronization), and this becomes challenging in modern inference engines with asynchronous scheduling mechanisms, thus conflicting with these methods. Some online conformal prediction algorithms <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Areces et al., </a>; <a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bhatnagar et al., 2023</a>)</cite> attempt to ensure the coverage of future data in the context of online learning.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Experimental Setup</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate a diverse set of draft models, including DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-1.5B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Guo et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Llama-8B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Guo et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">Team, 2024</a>)</cite>, Llama-3.1-8B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dubey et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, s1.1-7B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Muennighoff et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, and Skywork-OR1-7B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">He et al., 2025</a>)</cite>. Each draft model is paired with one of the large target models: QwQ-32B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">Team, 2025</a>)</cite>, s1.1-32B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Muennighoff et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, Qwen2.5-32B-Instruct <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">Team, 2024</a>)</cite>, DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-32B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Guo et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, or Skywork-OR1-32B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">He et al., 2025</a>)</cite>. We use SpecReason <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">Pan et al., 2025b</a>)</cite> and Speculative Thinking <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang et al., 2025</a>)</cite> as baselines for speculative decoding, with a maximum length of 8192. Both of them focus on acceleration under serial scaling.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Our evaluation covers four reasoning benchmarks. We use 100 randomly sampled problems from MATH <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hendrycks et al., 2021</a>)</cite> (denoted as MATH100) for grade-school arithmetic word problems, AIME24 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Art of Problem Solving, </a>)</cite> and AIME25 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">OpenCompass, </a>)</cite> for high-school competition-level mathematics, and the first 50 problems from AMC23 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">math-ai, </a>)</cite> for the American Mathematics Competitions. These datasets require multi-step reasoning and are particularly suitable for testing the effectiveness of asynchronous sampling with rejection. To ensure consistency, we set a token budget of 8192 across all settings and adopt deterministic decoding with temperature set to zero.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Similar to prior
work <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yue et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, the best@16 metric we calculate is intended to measure the upper bound of performance for both the method and the baseline model. Unless otherwise specified, the miscoverage parameter is set to <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0.4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0.4</annotation></semantics></math>, ensuring that the prediction sets are constructed with statistical guarantees. We use SGLang <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib49" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zheng et al., 2024</a>)</cite> version 0.4.3.post4 as the inference engine. The sampling temperature is set to 0.8. We set the target model’s per-turn token budget to <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{t}=500" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>500</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{t}=500</annotation></semantics></math> and the draft model’s per-turn token budget to <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{d}=500" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>500</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{d}=500</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Controlling the rejection rate in multi-turn interactions</h3>

<figure id="A1.F9" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A1.F9.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.15148v1/E4_ppl_line.svg" id="A1.F9.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/365;" width="548" height="365"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span>PPL variation with increasing turns.</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A1.F9.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.15148v1/E4_take_over_counts.svg" id="A1.F9.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/365;" width="548" height="365"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span>Take-over counts across multiple turns.</figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 9: </span>Analysis of model behavior in multi-turn interactions. The left subfigure shows how the Perplexity (PPL) of draft and target models evolves as the number of turns increases, while the right subfigure presents the take-over counts across turns.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we study the variation of model perplexity with sequential scaling and the change in the number of take-overs by the large model during rejection sampling. This directly reflects whether the conformal prediction algorithm we adopt can control the intervention rate of the target model within an acceptable range. i): According to Figure <a href="#A1.F9.sf1" title="In Figure 9 ‣ A.3 Controlling the rejection rate in multi-turn interactions ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ A1: Asynchronous Test-Time Scaling via Conformal Prediction" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9(a)</span></a>, each generation by the draft model leads to an increase in the overall PPL, while the intervention of the target model effectively mitigates this trend. As the number of turns increases, the PPL of the scaling process can be gradually reduced, which indirectly results in a decrease in the rejection rate. ii): Meanwhile, in Figure <a href="#A1.F9.sf2" title="In Figure 9 ‣ A.3 Controlling the rejection rate in multi-turn interactions ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ A1: Asynchronous Test-Time Scaling via Conformal Prediction" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9(b)</span></a>, we directly visualize the change in the number of take-overs by the target model as the number of interaction turns increases. We observe that with sequential scaling, the target model overall maintains a rejection rate around a fixed level, which gradually decreases and eventually approaches zero. iii): The target model continuously adjusts the convergence behavior of the draft model’s perplexity during sequential scaling.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>Definition and Proof</h3>

<div id="Thmproposition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproposition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 1</span></span><span id="Thmproposition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmproposition1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmproposition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(X_{i},Y_{i})\}_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(X_{i},Y_{i})\}_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> are exchangeable random variables from the test dataset, and <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi\sim\text{Uniform}\{1,2,\ldots,n\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Uniform</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi\sim\text{Uniform}\{1,2,\ldots,n\}</annotation></semantics></math> represents randomly sampling one data point from the test dataset, where <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th sample of that data point, then the marginal conformal <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>-values defined as,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\xi}^{k}=\frac{\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sum_{j=1}^{m}\mathbf{1}(s_{\xi}^{k}\leq s_{i}^{j})+1}{nm+1}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\xi}^{k}=\frac{\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sum_{j=1}^{m}\mathbf{1}(s_{\xi}^{k}\leq s_{i}^{j})+1}{nm+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproposition1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">is valid in the sense that for the miscoverage rate <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(p_{\xi}^{k}\leq\alpha)\leq\alpha." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(p_{\xi}^{k}\leq\alpha)\leq\alpha.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproposition1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Moreover, if the conformity scores <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{s_{i}^{j}\}_{i=1,j=1}^{n,m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{s_{i}^{j}\}_{i=1,j=1}^{n,m}</annotation></semantics></math> are distinct surely, we have,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\xi}^{k}\sim U\left\{\frac{1}{nm+1},\frac{2}{nm+1},\ldots,1\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\xi}^{k}\sim U\left\{\frac{1}{nm+1},\frac{2}{nm+1},\ldots,1\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Proposition 1.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Suppose, for any given values of conformity scores, <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{1},\ldots,v_{nm+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{1},\ldots,v_{nm+1}</annotation></semantics></math>, they can be rearranged as <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{v}_{1}&lt;\cdots&lt;\tilde{v}_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">&lt;</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">&lt;</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{v}_{1}&lt;\cdots&lt;\tilde{v}_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> with repetitions <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{v}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{v}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{\ell}n_{i}=nm+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{\ell}n_{i}=nm+1</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the event of <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{s_{1}^{1},s_{1}^{2},\ldots,s_{n}^{m},s_{\xi}^{k}\}=\{v_{1},\ldots,v_{nm+1}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>m</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{s_{1}^{1},s_{1}^{2},\ldots,s_{n}^{m},s_{\xi}^{k}\}=\{v_{1},\ldots,v_{nm+1}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Then, under <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{v}</annotation></semantics></math>, for <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\ldots,\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\ldots,\ell</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(s_{\xi}^{k}=\tilde{v}_{i}\mid E_{v})=\frac{n_{i}}{nm+1}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(s_{\xi}^{k}=\tilde{v}_{i}\mid E_{v})=\frac{n_{i}}{nm+1},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">due to the exchangeability of conformity scores.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">We also note that under <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\xi}^{k}=\tilde{v}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\xi}^{k}=\tilde{v}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> we have from Equation equation <a href="#A1.E17" title="In Proposition 1. ‣ A.4 Definition and Proof ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ A1: Asynchronous Test-Time Scaling via Conformal Prediction" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\xi}^{k}=\frac{\sum_{l=1}^{i}n_{l}}{nm+1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\xi}^{k}=\frac{\sum_{l=1}^{i}n_{l}}{nm+1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Then, for any <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\ldots,\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\ldots,\ell</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(p_{\xi}^{k}\leq\alpha\mid E_{v},s_{\xi}^{k}=\tilde{v}_{i})=\begin{cases}0&amp;\text{if }\alpha&lt;\frac{\sum_{l=1}^{i}n_{l}}{nm+1},\\
1&amp;\text{otherwise}.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mstyle><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>otherwise</mtext><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(p_{\xi}^{k}\leq\alpha\mid E_{v},s_{\xi}^{k}=\tilde{v}_{i})=\begin{cases}0&amp;\text{if }\alpha&lt;\frac{\sum_{l=1}^{i}n_{l}}{nm+1},\\
1&amp;\text{otherwise}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, for any <math id="A1.SS4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\ldots,\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\ldots,\ell</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\sum_{l=1}^{i-1}n_{l}}{nm+1}\leq\alpha&lt;\frac{\sum_{l=1}^{i}n_{l}}{nm+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mstyle><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\sum_{l=1}^{i-1}n_{l}}{nm+1}\leq\alpha&lt;\frac{\sum_{l=1}^{i}n_{l}}{nm+1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(p_{\xi}^{k}\leq\alpha\mid E_{v})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(p_{\xi}^{k}\leq\alpha\mid E_{v})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{l=1}^{\ell}\mathbb{P}(p_{\xi}^{k}\leq\alpha\mid E_{v},s_{\xi}^{k}=\tilde{v}_{l})\cdot\mathbb{P}(s_{\xi}^{k}=\tilde{v}_{l}\mid E_{v})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{l=1}^{\ell}\mathbb{P}(p_{\xi}^{k}\leq\alpha\mid E_{v},s_{\xi}^{k}=\tilde{v}_{l})\cdot\mathbb{P}(s_{\xi}^{k}=\tilde{v}_{l}\mid E_{v})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\sum_{l=1}^{i-1}n_{l}}{nm+1}\leq\alpha." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≤</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\sum_{l=1}^{i-1}n_{l}}{nm+1}\leq\alpha.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">By taking the expectation over the above inequality, it follows that the conformal <math id="A1.SS4.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>-value <math id="A1.SS4.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\xi}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\xi}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is marginally valid.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Specifically, if conformity scores <math id="A1.SS4.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{s_{i}^{j}\}_{i=1,j=1}^{n,m}\cup\{s_{\xi}^{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{s_{i}^{j}\}_{i=1,j=1}^{n,m}\cup\{s_{\xi}^{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math> are distinct surely, then <math id="A1.SS4.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell=nm+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell=nm+1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS4.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{i}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{i}=1</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.SS4.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\ldots,nm+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\ldots,nm+1</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(p_{\xi}^{k}\leq\alpha\mid E_{v})=\frac{i-1}{nm+1},\quad\text{if }\frac{i-1}{nm+1}\leq\alpha&lt;\frac{i}{nm+1}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mi>i</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(p_{\xi}^{k}\leq\alpha\mid E_{v})=\frac{i-1}{nm+1},\quad\text{if }\frac{i-1}{nm+1}\leq\alpha&lt;\frac{i}{nm+1},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">that is, <math id="A1.SS4.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\xi}^{k}\mid E_{v}\sim U\left\{\frac{1}{nm+1},\frac{2}{nm+1},\ldots,1\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\xi}^{k}\mid E_{v}\sim U\left\{\frac{1}{nm+1},\frac{2}{nm+1},\ldots,1\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>. This completes the proof. Next, we address the theoretical part that guarantees conditional coverage.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmproposition2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproposition2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 2</span></span><span id="Thmproposition2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmproposition2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmproposition2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that <math id="Thmproposition2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(X_{i},Y_{i})\}_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(X_{i},Y_{i})\}_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> are exchangeable random variables from the test dataset, then for any sample <math id="Thmproposition2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math>, given a conditioning set <math id="Thmproposition2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{y}\subseteq\{0,\ldots,m-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{y}\subseteq\{0,\ldots,m-1\}</annotation></semantics></math> for each <math id="Thmproposition2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> constructed based on the specific sample <math id="Thmproposition2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> for a test input <math id="Thmproposition2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmproposition2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{\xi}=y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{\xi}=y</annotation></semantics></math>, the corresponding conditional conformal <math id="Thmproposition2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>-value as defined in Equation equation <a href="#A1.E17" title="In Proposition 1. ‣ A.4 Definition and Proof ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ A1: Asynchronous Test-Time Scaling via Conformal Prediction" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>, is conditionally valid in the sense that for any <math id="Thmproposition2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(p_{\xi}^{k}\leq\alpha\mid\mathcal{I}_{y},Y_{\xi}=y)\leq\alpha." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(p_{\xi}^{k}\leq\alpha\mid\mathcal{I}_{y},Y_{\xi}=y)\leq\alpha.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproposition2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Moreover, if <math id="Thmproposition2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{s_{i}^{j}\}_{j\in\mathcal{I}_{y},i=1,\ldots,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{s_{i}^{j}\}_{j\in\mathcal{I}_{y},i=1,\ldots,n}</annotation></semantics></math> are distinct surely, we have that conditional on <math id="Thmproposition2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmproposition2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{\xi}=y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{\xi}=y</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\xi}^{k}\sim U\left\{\frac{1}{m+1},\frac{2}{m+1},\ldots,1\right\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\xi}^{k}\sim U\left\{\frac{1}{m+1},\frac{2}{m+1},\ldots,1\right\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproposition2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmproposition2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=|\mathcal{I}_{y}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=|\mathcal{I}_{y}|</annotation></semantics></math> is the size of the conditioning set for output <math id="Thmproposition2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS4.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">For any given sample <math id="A1.SS4.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math>, the corresponding conditional conformal <math id="A1.SS4.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>-value is given by</span></p>
<table id="A1.E28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E28.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\xi}^{k}=\frac{1}{m+1}\left(\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sum_{j\in\mathcal{I}_{y}}\mathbf{1}\{s_{i}^{j}\leq s_{\xi}^{k}\}+1\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mrow><mo>(</mo><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\xi}^{k}=\frac{1}{m+1}\left(\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sum_{j\in\mathcal{I}_{y}}\mathbf{1}\{s_{i}^{j}\leq s_{\xi}^{k}\}+1\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A1.SS4.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{y}\subseteq\{0,\ldots,m-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{y}\subseteq\{0,\ldots,m-1\}</annotation></semantics></math> is the conditioning set for sample <math id="A1.SS4.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS4.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=|\mathcal{I}_{y}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=|\mathcal{I}_{y}|</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS4.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}^{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}^{j}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the conformity score for the <math id="A1.SS4.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>-th candidate of the <math id="A1.SS4.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th test instance, and <math id="A1.SS4.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\xi}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\xi}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is the conformity score for the <math id="A1.SS4.p8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th candidate of the new test instance.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Given <math id="A1.SS4.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS4.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{\xi}=y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{\xi}=y</annotation></semantics></math>, the conformity scores <math id="A1.SS4.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{s_{i}^{j}\}_{j\in\mathcal{I}_{y},i=1,\ldots,n}\cup\{s_{\xi}^{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{s_{i}^{j}\}_{j\in\mathcal{I}_{y},i=1,\ldots,n}\cup\{s_{\xi}^{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math> are exchangeably distributed, which follows from the assumption that <math id="A1.SS4.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(X_{i},Y_{i})\}_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(X_{i},Y_{i})\}_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> are exchangeably distributed and the construction of candidate outputs.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Using similar arguments as in the proof of Proposition 1, for any given values of conformity scores <math id="A1.SS4.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{1},\ldots,v_{nm+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{1},\ldots,v_{nm+1}</annotation></semantics></math>, suppose that they can be arranged as <math id="A1.SS4.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{v}_{1}&lt;\cdots&lt;\tilde{v}_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">&lt;</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">&lt;</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{v}_{1}&lt;\cdots&lt;\tilde{v}_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> with repetitions <math id="A1.SS4.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A1.SS4.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{v}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{v}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A1.SS4.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{\ell}m_{i}=nm+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{\ell}m_{i}=nm+1</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A1.SS4.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the event <math id="A1.SS4.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{s_{i}^{j}\}_{j\in\mathcal{I}_{y},i=1,\ldots,n}\cup\{s_{\xi}^{k}\}=\{v_{1},\ldots,v_{nm+1}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{s_{i}^{j}\}_{j\in\mathcal{I}_{y},i=1,\ldots,n}\cup\{s_{\xi}^{k}\}=\{v_{1},\ldots,v_{nm+1}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Then, given <math id="A1.SS4.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{v}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS4.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{y}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS4.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{\xi}=y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{\xi}=y</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.E29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(s_{\xi}^{k}=\tilde{v}_{i}\mid E_{v},\mathcal{I}_{y},Y_{\xi}=y)=\frac{m_{i}}{nm+1}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(s_{\xi}^{k}=\tilde{v}_{i}\mid E_{v},\mathcal{I}_{y},Y_{\xi}=y)=\frac{m_{i}}{nm+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p11.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p11.2.1" class="ltx_text">for <math id="A1.SS4.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\ldots,\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\ldots,\ell</annotation></semantics></math>, due to exchangeability of the conformity scores.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">Note that given <math id="A1.SS4.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{v}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS4.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{y}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS4.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{\xi}=y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{\xi}=y</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS4.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\xi}^{k}=\tilde{v}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\xi}^{k}=\tilde{v}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have from Equation equation <a href="#A1.E28" title="In Proof. ‣ A.4 Definition and Proof ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ A1: Asynchronous Test-Time Scaling via Conformal Prediction" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\xi}^{k}=\frac{\sum_{j=1}^{i}m_{j}}{nm+1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\xi}^{k}=\frac{\sum_{j=1}^{i}m_{j}}{nm+1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p13" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, for any <math id="A1.SS4.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS4.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\ldots,\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\ldots,\ell</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(p_{\xi}^{k}\leq\alpha\mid E_{v},\mathcal{I}_{y},Y_{\xi}=y,s_{\xi}^{k}=\tilde{v}_{i})=\begin{cases}0&amp;\text{if }\alpha&lt;\frac{\sum_{j=1}^{i}m_{j}}{nm+1},\\
1&amp;\text{otherwise}.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mstyle><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>otherwise</mtext><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(p_{\xi}^{k}\leq\alpha\mid E_{v},\mathcal{I}_{y},Y_{\xi}=y,s_{\xi}^{k}=\tilde{v}_{i})=\begin{cases}0&amp;\text{if }\alpha&lt;\frac{\sum_{j=1}^{i}m_{j}}{nm+1},\\
1&amp;\text{otherwise}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p14" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">Then, for any given <math id="A1.SS4.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\ldots,\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\ldots,\ell</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS4.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\sum_{j=1}^{i-1}m_{j}}{nm+1}\leq\alpha&lt;\frac{\sum_{j=1}^{i}m_{j}}{nm+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mstyle><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\sum_{j=1}^{i-1}m_{j}}{nm+1}\leq\alpha&lt;\frac{\sum_{j=1}^{i}m_{j}}{nm+1}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(p_{\xi}^{k}\leq\alpha\mid E_{v},\mathcal{I}_{y},Y_{\xi}=y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(p_{\xi}^{k}\leq\alpha\mid E_{v},\mathcal{I}_{y},Y_{\xi}=y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{j=1}^{\ell}\mathbb{P}(p_{\xi}^{k}\leq\alpha\mid E_{v},\mathcal{I}_{y},Y_{\xi}=y,s_{\xi}^{k}=\tilde{v}_{j})\cdot\mathbb{P}(s_{\xi}^{k}=\tilde{v}_{j}\mid E_{v},\mathcal{I}_{y},Y_{\xi}=y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>v</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{j=1}^{\ell}\mathbb{P}(p_{\xi}^{k}\leq\alpha\mid E_{v},\mathcal{I}_{y},Y_{\xi}=y,s_{\xi}^{k}=\tilde{v}_{j})\cdot\mathbb{P}(s_{\xi}^{k}=\tilde{v}_{j}\mid E_{v},\mathcal{I}_{y},Y_{\xi}=y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\sum_{j=1}^{i-1}m_{j}}{nm+1}\leq\alpha." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≤</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\sum_{j=1}^{i-1}m_{j}}{nm+1}\leq\alpha.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">By taking expectation, it follows that <math id="A1.SS4.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\xi}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\xi}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is conditionally valid given <math id="A1.SS4.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{\xi}=y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{\xi}=y</annotation></semantics></math>. This completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Discussion.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">After proving the validity of individual conformal p-values, in order to obtain the rejection rate for the entire test set, that is, to ensure that the overall error rate is controlled when simultaneously testing K hypotheses, we propose the following Proposition.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproposition3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproposition3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 3</span></span><span id="Thmproposition3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmproposition3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmproposition3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that <math id="Thmproposition3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(X_{i},Y_{i})\}_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(X_{i},Y_{i})\}_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> are exchangeable random variables, and let <math id="Thmproposition3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi\sim\text{Uniform}\{1,2,\ldots,n\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Uniform</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi\sim\text{Uniform}\{1,2,\ldots,n\}</annotation></semantics></math> represent a randomly selected test instance, then <span id="Thmproposition3.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">A1</span> based on marginal conformal <math id="Thmproposition3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>-values all provide simultaneous coverage guarantees across the entire test dataset at level <math id="Thmproposition3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e.,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E35.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}(\forall i\in\{1,\ldots,n\}:Y_{i}\in\mathcal{C}(X_{i}))\geq 1-\alpha." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(\forall i\in\{1,\ldots,n\}:Y_{i}\in\mathcal{C}(X_{i}))\geq 1-\alpha.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproposition3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Specifically, if the conformity scores <math id="Thmproposition3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{s_{i}^{j}\}_{i=1,j=1}^{n,m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{s_{i}^{j}\}_{i=1,j=1}^{n,m}</annotation></semantics></math> are distinct surely, then for <span id="Thmproposition3.p1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">A1</span>, we also have,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E36.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}(\forall i\in\{1,\ldots,n\}:Y_{i}\in\mathcal{C}(X_{i}))\geq 1-\alpha+\frac{1}{(n-1)m+1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(\forall i\in\{1,\ldots,n\}:Y_{i}\in\mathcal{C}(X_{i}))\geq 1-\alpha+\frac{1}{(n-1)m+1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Proposition 3.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Consider <span id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">A1</span> based on marginal conformal <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>-values. Note that among the tested hypotheses <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{1},\ldots,H_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{1},\ldots,H_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, there is exactly one hypothesis <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{Y_{\xi}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{Y_{\xi}}</annotation></semantics></math> to be true. Thus, the probability that all samples are correctly covered by <span id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">A1</span> satisfies:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E37.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(\forall i\in\{1,\ldots,n\}:Y_{i}\in\mathcal{C}(X_{i}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(\forall i\in\{1,\ldots,n\}:Y_{i}\in\mathcal{C}(X_{i}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E37.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}(\text{accept }H_{Y_{\xi}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>accept </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}(\text{accept }H_{Y_{\xi}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=1-\mathbb{P}(\text{reject }H_{Y_{\xi}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>reject </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=1-\mathbb{P}(\text{reject }H_{Y_{\xi}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq 1-\mathbb{P}(p_{\xi}^{Y_{\xi}}\leq\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>ξ</mi><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq 1-\mathbb{P}(p_{\xi}^{Y_{\xi}}\leq\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq 1-\alpha," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq 1-\alpha,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the last inequality follows by Proposition 1.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Specifically, for <span id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">A1</span>, if the conformity scores <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{s_{i}^{j}\}_{i=1,j=1}^{n,m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{s_{i}^{j}\}_{i=1,j=1}^{n,m}</annotation></semantics></math> are distinct surely, by Proposition 1, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E41.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(\forall i\in\{1,\ldots,n\}:Y_{i}\in\mathcal{C}(X_{i}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(\forall i\in\{1,\ldots,n\}:Y_{i}\in\mathcal{C}(X_{i}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E41.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}(\text{accept }H_{Y_{\xi}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>accept </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}(\text{accept }H_{Y_{\xi}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=1-\mathbb{P}(p_{\xi}^{Y_{\xi}}\leq\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>ξ</mi><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=1-\mathbb{P}(p_{\xi}^{Y_{\xi}}\leq\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq 1-\left(\alpha-\frac{1}{(n-1)m+1}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq 1-\left(\alpha-\frac{1}{(n-1)m+1}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=1-\alpha+\frac{1}{(n-1)m+1}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=1-\alpha+\frac{1}{(n-1)m+1},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(44)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">which gives the desired result.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(X_{i},Y_{i})\}_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(X_{i},Y_{i})\}_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> are exchangeable random variables, and let <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi\sim\text{Uniform}\{1,2,\ldots,n\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Uniform</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi\sim\text{Uniform}\{1,2,\ldots,n\}</annotation></semantics></math> represent a randomly selected test instance, then the prediction set <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}(X_{\xi})=\left\{\hat{Y}_{\xi}^{k}\mid p_{\xi}^{k}&gt;\alpha\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ξ</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}(X_{\xi})=\left\{\hat{Y}_{\xi}^{k}\mid p_{\xi}^{k}&gt;\alpha\right\}</annotation></semantics></math> determined by <span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">A1</span> both satisfy</span></p>
<table id="A1.E45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(Y_{\xi}\in\mathcal{C}(X_{\xi}))\geq 1-\alpha." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(Y_{\xi}\in\mathcal{C}(X_{\xi}))\geq 1-\alpha.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(45)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Note that the prediction set is given by <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}(X_{\xi})=A_{1}\cap A_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}(X_{\xi})=A_{1}\cap A_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, by Proposition 1,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(Y_{\xi}\in\mathcal{C}(X_{\xi}))\geq\mathbb{P}(p_{\xi}^{Y_{\xi}}&gt;\alpha)\geq 1-\alpha." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>ξ</mi><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(Y_{\xi}\in\mathcal{C}(X_{\xi}))\geq\mathbb{P}(p_{\xi}^{Y_{\xi}}&gt;\alpha)\geq 1-\alpha.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(46)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Similarly, its prediction set is given by</span></p>
<table id="A1.E47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}(X_{\xi})=\{y\in\mathcal{Y}:p_{\xi}^{y}&gt;\alpha\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>y</mi></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}(X_{\xi})=\{y\in\mathcal{Y}:p_{\xi}^{y}&gt;\alpha\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(47)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">By Proposition 1, it is easy to check that</span></p>
<table id="A1.E48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(Y_{\xi}\in\mathcal{C}(X_{\xi}))=\mathbb{P}(p_{\xi}^{Y_{\xi}}&gt;\alpha)\geq 1-\alpha." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>ξ</mi><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(Y_{\xi}\in\mathcal{C}(X_{\xi}))=\mathbb{P}(p_{\xi}^{Y_{\xi}}&gt;\alpha)\geq 1-\alpha.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(48)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Specifically, if the conformity scores <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{s_{i}^{j}\}_{i=1,j=1}^{n,m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{s_{i}^{j}\}_{i=1,j=1}^{n,m}</annotation></semantics></math> are distinct surely, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.E49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(Y_{\xi}\in\mathcal{C}(X_{\xi}))=1-\mathbb{P}(p_{\xi}^{Y_{\xi}}\leq\alpha)\leq 1-\alpha+\frac{1}{(n-1)m+1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>ξ</mi><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(Y_{\xi}\in\mathcal{C}(X_{\xi}))=1-\mathbb{P}(p_{\xi}^{Y_{\xi}}\leq\alpha)\leq 1-\alpha+\frac{1}{(n-1)m+1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(49)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">This completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Discussion.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Now that we have completed the proof of marginal coverage, we proceed to prove the conditional coverage for the entire test dataset. Under the exchangeability assumption, we have:</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproposition4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproposition4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 4</span></span><span id="Thmproposition4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmproposition4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmproposition4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under the same exchangeability assumption as in Proposition 2, <span id="Thmproposition4.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">A1</span> based on conditional conformal <math id="Thmproposition4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>-values <math id="Thmproposition4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\xi}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\xi}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math> all provide conditional coverage guarantees for the entire test dataset at level <math id="Thmproposition4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., for any <math id="Thmproposition4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E50.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}(\forall i\in\{1,\ldots,n\}:Y_{i}\in\mathcal{C}(X_{i})\mid Y_{\xi}=y)\geq 1-\alpha." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(\forall i\in\{1,\ldots,n\}:Y_{i}\in\mathcal{C}(X_{i})\mid Y_{\xi}=y)\geq 1-\alpha.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(50)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproposition4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Specifically, if the conformity scores <math id="Thmproposition4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{s_{i}^{j}\}_{j\in\mathcal{I}_{y},i=1,\ldots,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{s_{i}^{j}\}_{j\in\mathcal{I}_{y},i=1,\ldots,n}</annotation></semantics></math> are distinct surely, then for <span id="Thmproposition4.p1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">A1</span> based on <math id="Thmproposition4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\xi}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\xi}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that for any <math id="Thmproposition4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmproposition4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{y}\subseteq\{0,\ldots,m-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{y}\subseteq\{0,\ldots,m-1\}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E51.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}(\forall i\in\{1,\ldots,n\}:Y_{i}\in\mathcal{C}(X_{i})\mid Y_{\xi}=y,\mathcal{I}_{y})\geq 1-\alpha+\frac{1}{(n-1)|\mathcal{I}_{y}|+1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(\forall i\in\{1,\ldots,n\}:Y_{i}\in\mathcal{C}(X_{i})\mid Y_{\xi}=y,\mathcal{I}_{y})\geq 1-\alpha+\frac{1}{(n-1)|\mathcal{I}_{y}|+1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(51)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Consider Procedure 1-3 based on conditional conformal <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>-values. For any <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math>, given <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{\xi}=y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{\xi}=y</annotation></semantics></math>, the conditional coverage probability for the entire test dataset satisfies:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E52.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(\forall i\in\{1,\ldots,n\}:Y_{i}\in\mathcal{C}(X_{i})\mid Y_{\xi}=y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(\forall i\in\{1,\ldots,n\}:Y_{i}\in\mathcal{C}(X_{i})\mid Y_{\xi}=y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E52.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=1-\mathbb{P}(\text{reject }H_{y}\mid Y_{\xi}=y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>reject </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=1-\mathbb{P}(\text{reject }H_{y}\mid Y_{\xi}=y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(52)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq 1-\mathbb{P}(p_{\xi}^{y}\leq\alpha\mid Y_{\xi}=y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>y</mi></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq 1-\mathbb{P}(p_{\xi}^{y}\leq\alpha\mid Y_{\xi}=y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(53)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq 1-\alpha," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq 1-\alpha,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(54)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the inequalities follow from the definitions of Procedure 1-3 and Proposition 2.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Specifically, for Procedure 3, if the conformity scores <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{s_{i}^{j}\}_{j\in\mathcal{I}_{y},i=1,\ldots,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{s_{i}^{j}\}_{j\in\mathcal{I}_{y},i=1,\ldots,n}</annotation></semantics></math> are distinct surely, then by Proposition 2, the coverage probability conditional on <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{\xi}=y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{\xi}=y</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E55.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(\forall i\in\{1,\ldots,n\}:Y_{i}\in\mathcal{C}(X_{i})\mid\mathcal{I}_{y},Y_{\xi}=y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(\forall i\in\{1,\ldots,n\}:Y_{i}\in\mathcal{C}(X_{i})\mid\mathcal{I}_{y},Y_{\xi}=y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E55.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=1-\mathbb{P}(\text{reject }H_{y}\mid\mathcal{I}_{y},Y_{\xi}=y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>reject </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=1-\mathbb{P}(\text{reject }H_{y}\mid\mathcal{I}_{y},Y_{\xi}=y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(55)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=1-\mathbb{P}(p_{\xi}^{y}\leq\alpha\mid\mathcal{I}_{y},Y_{\xi}=y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>y</mi></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=1-\mathbb{P}(p_{\xi}^{y}\leq\alpha\mid\mathcal{I}_{y},Y_{\xi}=y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(56)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E57"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq 1-\left(\alpha-\frac{1}{(n-1)|\mathcal{I}_{y}|+1}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq 1-\left(\alpha-\frac{1}{(n-1)|\mathcal{I}_{y}|+1}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(57)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E58"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=1-\alpha+\frac{1}{(n-1)|\mathcal{I}_{y}|+1}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=1-\alpha+\frac{1}{(n-1)|\mathcal{I}_{y}|+1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(58)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">This completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 2</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under the same exchangeability assumption as in Theorem 1, the prediction set <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}(X_{\xi}\mid y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}(X_{\xi}\mid y)</annotation></semantics></math> based on conditional conformal <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>-values <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\xi}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\xi}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A1.E59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(Y_{\xi}\in\mathcal{C}(X_{\xi}\mid y)\mid Y_{\xi}=y)\geq 1-\alpha" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(Y_{\xi}\in\mathcal{C}(X_{\xi}\mid y)\mid Y_{\xi}=y)\geq 1-\alpha</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(59)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">for any <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math>. Specifically, for the prediction set <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}(X_{\xi}\mid y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}(X_{\xi}\mid y)</annotation></semantics></math> based on <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\xi}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\xi}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, if the conformity scores <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{s_{i}^{j}\}_{j\in\mathcal{I}_{y},i=1,\ldots,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{s_{i}^{j}\}_{j\in\mathcal{I}_{y},i=1,\ldots,n}</annotation></semantics></math> are distinct surely, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.E60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(Y_{\xi}\in\mathcal{C}(X_{\xi}\mid y)\mid Y_{\xi}=y,\mathcal{I}_{y})\leq 1-\alpha+\frac{1}{(n-1)|\mathcal{I}_{y}|+1}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(Y_{\xi}\in\mathcal{C}(X_{\xi}\mid y)\mid Y_{\xi}=y,\mathcal{I}_{y})\leq 1-\alpha+\frac{1}{(n-1)|\mathcal{I}_{y}|+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(60)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">for any <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{y}\subseteq\{0,\ldots,m-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{y}\subseteq\{0,\ldots,m-1\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">By using Proposition 4 and similar arguments as in the proof of Theorem 1, the prediction sets <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}(X_{\xi}\mid y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}(X_{\xi}\mid y)</annotation></semantics></math> based on the conditional conformal <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>-values <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\xi}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\xi}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math> all satisfy:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(Y_{\xi}\in\mathcal{C}(X_{\xi}\mid y)\mid\mathcal{I}_{y},Y_{\xi}=y)\geq 1-\alpha" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(Y_{\xi}\in\mathcal{C}(X_{\xi}\mid y)\mid\mathcal{I}_{y},Y_{\xi}=y)\geq 1-\alpha</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(61)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">for any <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Specifically, if the conformity scores <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{s_{i}^{j}\}_{j\in\mathcal{I}_{y},i=1,\ldots,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{s_{i}^{j}\}_{j\in\mathcal{I}_{y},i=1,\ldots,n}</annotation></semantics></math> are distinct surely, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E62"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(Y_{\xi}\in\mathcal{C}(X_{\xi}\mid y)\mid\mathcal{I}_{y},Y_{\xi}=y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(Y_{\xi}\in\mathcal{C}(X_{\xi}\mid y)\mid\mathcal{I}_{y},Y_{\xi}=y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E62.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}(p_{\xi}^{y}&gt;\alpha\mid\mathcal{I}_{y},Y_{\xi}=y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>ξ</mi><mi>y</mi></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>ξ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{P}(p_{\xi}^{y}&gt;\alpha\mid\mathcal{I}_{y},Y_{\xi}=y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(62)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E63"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 1-\alpha+\frac{1}{(n-1)|\mathcal{I}_{y}|+1}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 1-\alpha+\frac{1}{(n-1)|\mathcal{I}_{y}|+1},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(63)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">which gives the desired result.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
